{"title":"2000 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45352cfe3b341ec6adbd489654cd9175766486bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AH_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/4723076e6ad29aeeddb0a2d9f76af3fbe3b3155a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BH_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50caa7f42d1efff7a321994184e649bffd72386b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CH_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"21\" /> be the altitudes of an acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.  The incircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> touches the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d8e9c5c70be5e8b812a08ce2566d0db946c608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, respectively.  Consider the reflections of the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/e/b7e54f0551e7a2a8afe80e1c82ffdf76cbf96b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_1H_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552e7b2081eb57d63c3d77a1c1cb017b04b540ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_2H_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a354eb29d0e3d4e81f5bb5d61532e5eddcd1ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_3H_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> with respect to the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74dfa07abb8b287e381220e1d94def3db9b2b7d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55f2691555c1e850d8ed2813c4ad9ce28ff54ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2T_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce782284f74319edbfe76f58afbc7d5be6f1742e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_3T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />.  Prove that these images form a triangle whose vertices lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f503e5181c5462f2a1f5a472a6a8a084e5573c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(300); // Settings for fonts and line styles defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)); pen normal_pen = black + 0.4pt; pen dashed_pen = linetype(&quot;4 4&quot;) + black;  // Helper functions for geometry projection and reflection pair project(pair P, pair A, pair B) {     pair v = B - A;     return A + dot(P - A, v) / dot(v, v) * v; }  pair reflect_pt(pair P, pair A, pair B) {     return 2 * project(P, A, B) - P; }  void draw_right_angle(pair V, pair A, pair B, real size=0.2, pen p=normal_pen) {     pair u = unit(A - V) * size;     pair v = unit(B - V) * size;     draw(V + u -- V + u + v -- V + v, p); }  // Function to extend line segment PQ past both ends: path extend_line(pair P, pair Q, real t1=2.0, real t2=2.0) {     pair u = unit(Q - P);     return (P - t1 * u) -- (Q + t2 * u); }  // Initial conditions: Acute triangle with Angle B = 70 deg, Angle C = 60 deg real angleB = 70; real angleC = 60; real angleA = 180 - angleB - angleC; // 50 deg real a = 8; // base length BC  real c = a * sin(angleC * pi / 180) / sin(angleA * pi / 180); real b = a * sin(angleB * pi / 180) / sin(angleA * pi / 180);  // Vertices of Triangle ABC pair B = (0, 0); pair C = (a, 0); pair A = (c * cos(angleB * pi / 180), c * sin(angleB * pi / 180));  // Feet of Altitudes (lying directly on the sides since ABC is acute) pair H1 = project(A, B, C); // On side BC pair H2 = project(B, A, C); // On side CA pair H3 = project(C, A, B); // On side AB  // Incircle parameters pair I = (a*A + b*B + c*C) / (a + b + c); real s = (a + b + c) / 2; real r = sqrt((s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c) / s); path omega = circle(I, r);  // Tangency points on sides BC, CA, AB pair T1 = project(I, B, C); pair T2 = project(I, A, C); pair T3 = project(I, A, B);  // Reflections pair H1_prime = reflect_pt(H1, T1, T2); pair H2_prime = reflect_pt(H2, T1, T2);  pair H2_star = reflect_pt(H2, T2, T3); pair H3_star = reflect_pt(H3, T2, T3);  pair H3_dprime = reflect_pt(H3, T3, T1); pair H1_dprime = reflect_pt(H1, T3, T1);  // Intersection point D = H1&#39;H2&#39; \\cap H2*H3* pair D = extension(H1_prime, H2_prime, H2_star, H3_star);  // --- DRAWING ELEMENTS ---  // 1. Draw Triangle ABC draw(A--B--C--cycle, normal_pen);  // 2. Draw Incircle draw(omega, normal_pen);  // 3. Draw Dashed Altitudes draw(A--H1, dashed_pen); // Altitude AH1 draw(B--H2, dashed_pen); // Altitude BH2 draw(C--H3, dashed_pen); // Altitude CH3  // 4. Right angle marks draw_right_angle(H1, A, C, 0.2, normal_pen); draw_right_angle(H2, B, A, 0.2, normal_pen); draw_right_angle(H3, C, B, 0.2, normal_pen);  // 5. Connect feet of perpendiculars (Orthic Triangle) draw(H1--H2, normal_pen); draw(H2--H3, normal_pen); draw(H3--H1, normal_pen);  // 6. Connect tangency points (Incenter Triangle) draw(T1--T2, normal_pen); draw(T2--T3, normal_pen); draw(T3--T1, normal_pen);  // 7. Reflected segments draw(H1_prime--H2_prime, normal_pen); draw(H2_star--H3_star, normal_pen);  // --- OPTIONAL LINE EXTENSIONS --- draw(extend_line(H1_prime, H2_prime, 0.4, 2.5), normal_pen + gray); draw(extend_line(H2_star, H3_star, 2.0, 1.5), normal_pen + gray); draw(extend_line(T1, T2, 0.5, 1.5), normal_pen + gray); draw(extend_line(T2, T3, 1.0, 1.5), normal_pen + gray);  // --- DOTS AND LABELS --- dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE);  dot(&quot;$H_1$&quot;, H1, S); dot(&quot;$H_2$&quot;, H2, E); dot(&quot;$H_3$&quot;, H3, NW);  dot(&quot;$T_1$&quot;, T1, S); dot(&quot;$T_2$&quot;, T2, E); dot(&quot;$T_3$&quot;, T3, NW);  dot(&quot;$H_1&#39;$&quot;, H1_prime, SE); dot(&quot;$H_2&#39;$&quot;, H2_prime, NW); dot(&quot;$H_2^*$&quot;, H2_star, NE); dot(&quot;$H_3^*$&quot;, H3_star, NW);  // Dot and label for Intersection D (lying on omega) dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, N);  label(&quot;$\\omega$&quot;, I + r*dir(200), SW);  // Shipout image shipout(bbox(0.1cm, Fill(white))); [/asy]\" width=\"465\" height=\"498\" />\nWe establish a complex plane with the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> being the unit circle. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99a8878866427975b7412e2d870677cf049d1d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert p\\rvert=\\lvert q\\rvert=\\lvert r\\rvert=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" />. Let the lowercase letter of each point denote its complex coordinate (when not specified). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/590a14c7558ddc9df29535c542042e82935e937a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1=p, t_2=q, t_3=r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"17\" />. We know that\n\\begin{gather*}\na=\\frac{2qr}{q+r}, \\quad b=\\frac{2rp}{r+p},\\quad c=\\frac{2pq}{p+q}\\\\\n\\bar a=\\frac{2}{q+r}, \\quad \\bar b=\\frac{2}{r+p}, \\quad \\bar c=\\frac{2}{p+q}\n\\end{gather*}\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265249bd0c1265918b1d92838b1980a2f4d5619f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1=\\frac{b(\\bar a-\\bar c)-c(\\bar a-\\bar b)}{2(\\bar b-\\bar c)}+\\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"229\" height=\"47\" />. Substituting the above expressions yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366650104609d5c162f9902508a18f44d52b3925.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h_1=\\frac{pq+qr+rp-p^2}{q+r}\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"43\" />\nSimilarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb3046a4e9dd5c79f2272aba756eab6cee3364c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2=\\frac{pq+qr+rp-q^2}{r+p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"184\" height=\"44\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f066d473da7892bee9cdd148bfabaaf1b37aec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1&#39;,h_2&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> be the reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1fe6d255e3f93ad3387548675d1447c0f28cee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_1,H_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74dfa07abb8b287e381220e1d94def3db9b2b7d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, respectively. The point of reflection formula gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87422ce96948ab40a99a5e80926f5cfe3aaae51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h_1&#39;=\\frac{\\bar p q-p\\bar q+\\bar{h_1}(p-q)}{\\bar p-\\bar q}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"44\" />\nSubstituting, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/9116027f128ed83d6499f137c8fbb2ec796c7ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1&#39;=\\frac{r(p^2+q^2)}{p(q+r)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"126\" height=\"45\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb431ce11cfbe7983ff84f776eb1b800b844b08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2&#39;=\\frac{r(p^2+q^2)}{q(r+p)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"126\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8b6a6323d7b0bf9d9f1d56b12d0d608fae2e035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2^*,h_3^*$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" /> be the reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecba9f85af6e3b1e1a558760853d6c9851563a58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_2,H_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55f2691555c1e850d8ed2813c4ad9ce28ff54ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2T_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />. By symmetry,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff23c504c7021f6816de6674a6fd3efd42096d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h_2^*=\\frac{p(q^2+r^2)}{q(r+p)},\\quad h_3^*=\\frac{p(q^2+r^2)}{r(p+q)}\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"44\" />\nWe have the equations of the two lines:\n\\begin{align*}\n(\\overline{h_1'}-\\overline{h_2'})z-(h_1'-h_2')\\overline{z}&amp;=\\overline{h_1'}h_2'-h_1'\\overline{h_2'}\\\\\n(\\overline{h_2^*}-\\overline{h_3^*})z-(h_2^*-h_3^*)\\overline{z}&amp;=\\overline{h_2^*}h_3^*-h_2^*\\overline{h_3^*}\n\\end{align*}\nLet \n\\begin{gather*}\nS_p=p+q,\\quad S_q=q+r,\\quad S_r=r+p\\\\\nS_{p^2}=p^2+q^2,\\quad S_{q^2}=q^2+r^2,\\quad S_{r^2}=r^2+p^2\n\\end{gather*}\nWe have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c630a3766a6c9790c04fb73a4c3c47fe852c90da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline{h_1^{\\prime}}-\\overline{h_2^{\\prime}}=\\frac{S_{p^2}}{pqS_q}-\\frac{S_{p^2}}{pqS_r}=\\frac{S_{p^2}(p-q)}{pqS_qS_r}\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"43\" />\nAlso,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed1bdc4145301f7e0201d38beb9f121728daa286.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h_1&#39;-h_2&#39;=\\frac{rS_{p^2}}{pS_q}-\\frac{rS_{p^2}}{qS_r}=\\frac{r^2S_{p^2}(q-p)}{pqS_qS_r}\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"44\" />\nEvaluating the RHS of the line equation, we see that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9156435b37de228381e23a6fba90909e9b2b34cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overline{h_1&#39;}h_2&#39;-h_1&#39;\\overline{h_2&#39;}=\\frac{rS_{p^2}^2}{pq^2S_qS_r}-\\frac{rS_{p^2}^2}{p^2qS_qS_r}=\\frac{rS_{p^2}^2(p-q)}{p^2q^2S_qS_r}\\]\" width=\"388\" height=\"46\" />\nAs we substitute those coefficients into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587edad44bc07186584e2522b8fe2769515b4065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />, dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e0b865e2e7b9a88d89e32d8853a287cc219a3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S_{p^2}(p-q)}{pqS_qS_r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"85\" height=\"45\" /> yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/01891a66f0270f3cc3159cd542e3033a7eb2efbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z+r^2\\bar z=\\frac{r}{pq}S_{p^2}\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"36\" />\nSimilarly, the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709185d5f7792bf4044651f2cd3ffdc8ceb8a15b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+p^2\\bar z=\\frac{p}{qr}S_{q^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0c4bc995d91abee549bc0b6c01ac821d369e23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=H_1&#39;H_2&#39;\\cap H_2^*H_3^*$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" />. Solving the above system yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091a80626a94858b2262ab0f2e14429afa842260.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{pr}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, which satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f208ec04f12dcb261023ba7e0b4053dc344485b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d\\cdot\\overline{d}=\\frac{pr}{q}\\cdot\\frac{q}{pr}=1,\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"36\" />\nmeaning it is on the unit circle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/794ce736990f46d0063a7440965d0a49b279b834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_3^@,H_1^@$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"22\" /> be the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c2fecf0e0d4f9f38223fa16e16aedd1315b6c2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_3,H_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce782284f74319edbfe76f58afbc7d5be6f1742e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_3T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />. By symmetry,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9fa35b476263c0041fa03be6f193af964635bfd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[H_2^*H_3^*\\cap H_3^@H_1^@=\\frac{qp}{r}, \\quad H_3^@H_1^@\\cap H_1&#39;H_2&#39;=\\frac{rq}{p},\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"36\" />\nwhich also lie on the unit circle, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO\" title=\"2000 IMO\">2000 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2000 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194031\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 287/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13591/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.236      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.236      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25809:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194031 and revision id 292228. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}